    "effective": "2026-10-04",
    "body": "## Terms Summary\n\nThese Terms of Use govern access to and use of websites, digital catalogues, quotation carts, and inquiry portals operated by Velocity Lab Innovation (\"VLI\", \"we\", \"us\", or \"our\"), including [velocity-lab.com](/) and associated subdomains. By browsing our portals, requesting equipment pricing, or communicating with VLI, you (\"User\" or \"Client\") agree to be bound by these Terms.\n\n## Catalogue Pricing and Quotation Disclaimer\n\nPrices and specifications displayed on the VLI online equipment catalogue at [velocity-lab.com/product](/product) serve strictly as preliminary reference points. Listed figures do not constitute a legally binding public offer to sell.\n\n| Stage | Document / Status | Legal Effect |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Online Catalogue Browse | Indicative Price Reference | Non-binding product overview. Subject to stock and currency updates. |\n| Quote Request / Cart | Client Equipment Enquiry | Request for quotation. No contract formed. |\n| Written VLI Quotation | Tailored Quotation / Pro-Forma | Binding commercial offer valid for 30 calendar days unless stated otherwise. |\n| Client Confirmation | Signed PO or Deposit Receipt | Binding sales or service contract formed under VLI Commercial Terms. |\n\nA binding purchase or service contract is formed only when VLI issues a formal written quotation or pro-forma invoice, and the client confirms acceptance via an authorized Purchase Order (PO), signed quote acceptance, or settlement of the agreed deposit.\n\n## Intellectual Property Rights\n\nAll content published across VLI portals—including software code, Smart Referee system algorithms, tracking workflows, technical schematics, 3D cage designs, course curriculum outlines, text, photography, and brand graphics—is the exclusive intellectual property of Velocity Lab Innovation or its hardware partners and is protected by Hong Kong and international copyright and trademark laws.\n\nUsers may view, download, and print catalogue materials solely for internal evaluation or institutional procurement review. Reproducing, reverse-engineering, modifying, distributing, or commercially exploiting VLI intellectual property without prior written consent is strictly prohibited.\n\n## Acceptable Use of Digital Portals\n\nUsers agree to use VLI portals strictly for lawful purposes and must not:\n\n- Submit fraudulent, misleading, or abusive equipment inquiries or quote requests.\n- Attempt to compromise website security, bypass technical access restrictions, or scrape portal data using automated tools.\n- Misrepresent affiliation with educational institutions, sports clubs, or government procurement bodies.\n\n## Accuracy of Technical Information\n\nVLI makes every reasonable effort to ensure that drone weights, motor KV ratings, flight times, battery capacities, and competition whitelist standards (e.g., FAI F9A-A and F9A-B) are accurate and current. However, manufacturers periodically modify raw components, cage molds, and firmware versions. Exact flight endurance, thrust, and telemetry performance may vary based on environmental conditions, pilot skill, and payload configuration.\n\n## Limitation of Liability\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted under Hong Kong law, VLI shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, consequential, special, or punitive damages arising from the use of, or inability to use, our digital portals or published materials.\n\nVLI does not warrant that website functions will be uninterrupted or error-free, or that server infrastructure is free of malicious software, although industry-standard security measures are actively maintained.\n\n## Third-Party Links and Services\n\nOur website may link to third-party services, including component manufacturers (e.g., Betaflight, ExpressLRS), international aeromodelling bodies, courier tracking platforms, and external video services. VLI exercises no editorial control over third-party websites and accepts no responsibility for their content, policies, or operating practices.\n\n## Governing Law and Jurisdiction\n\nThese Terms of Use and any non-contractual obligations arising out of or in connection with them shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region. All disputes arising under these Terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Courts of Hong Kong SAR.\n\n## General Terms\n\nIf any provision of these Terms is found to be invalid or unenforceable by a court of competent jurisdiction, the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect. VLI's failure to enforce any right or provision shall not constitute a waiver of future enforcement.\n\nVLI reserves the right to revise these Terms of Use at any time by updating this document. Continued use of the website following published updates constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms. For legal or commercial inquiries, contact [info@velocity-lab.com](mailto:info@velocity-lab.com)."
